7.3 Worker leases

Each worker task in WORK_QUEUE.json should have fields equivalent to:

task id

title

priority

phase

status: queued | leased | implementing | validating | review_pending | done | blocked | recovery_needed

assigned worker/session

lease timestamp

lease expiry

files/modules expected to be touched

acceptance criteria

dependencies

last checkpoint

validation result

reviewer state

A lease should be refreshed when meaningful work is happening.

If a worker session dies or disappears and its lease expires:

Astra marks the task recovery_needed.

Astra creates a recovery directive containing the task goal, last commit, dirty files, last checkpoint, tests already run, and known risks.

A new worker reads that directive, Git diff/status, relevant code, and continues from the existing work.

Do not restart the feature from zero unless the previous partial implementation is unsalvageable and the reason is documented.

